Not submitted upstream.
llama-moe-prefill.patch, 2026-11-11 (levers 1-4). Base: llama.cpp master 7592b61d3. Apply: git apply llama-moe-prefill.patch
Contents
  1. ggml-cuda/mmid.cu: mm_ids_helper_par. A 32-warp, two-pass, order-preserving MUL_MAT_ID routing sort, used at
     >= 256 tokens (GGML_CUDA_MMID_PAR_MIN). Outputs are bit-identical. mm_ids at 10k: 82 -> 26 ms.
  2. ggml-cuda/mmq.cu: GGML_CUDA_MMQ_ID_J=<J> sweep knob (unset = stock tile rule). Wider tiles were REFUTED
     (J=128 at ub 2048: expert MMQ 354 -> 395 ms), so no rule is baked in.
  3. ggml-cuda/batch-get.cu: a grow-only pinned+mapped staging buffer replaces the per-call cudaHostRegister of the
     destination in ggml_cuda_get_tensor_n. llama-server's 3 context checkpoints per prompt (112.6 MiB each) and its
     --cache-ram prompt save (401 MiB at 10k) each pinned a fresh buffer. The staged bytes are memcpy'd out (8 threads
     >= 32 MB). GGML_CUDA_BATCH_GET_STAGING=0 restores the old path. Spans above GGML_CUDA_BATCH_GET_STAGING_MAX_MIB
     (default 1024) use the old path. Pinned host memory held = the largest staged span (448 MiB with the RAM prompt
     cache on, 128 MiB with --cache-ram 0).
Measured (RTX 5090, a MoE GGUF (IQ1_M), all-VRAM, -t 8 -b 4096 -ub 2048, cold unique-nonce chat-completions
text, 3 reps x 2 alternating passes n=6). Engine = server prompt timer; wall = client tok/s.
                                       2.7k engine / wall      10k engine / wall
  stock                                4,272 / 3,771           5,924 / 5,342
  this patch                           5,114 / 4,711           6,455 / 6,061   (RAM prompt cache save ~80 ms outside)
  this patch, --cache-ram 0            4,889 / 4,849           6,383 / 6,322
  this patch, --cache-ram 0 -ctxcp 0   6,642 / 6,549           7,119 / 7,040   (no hybrid checkpoints)
  Decode, 128 tokens: 128.3 tok/s (stock 128.9): unchanged.
Correctness: test-backend-ops -o MUL_MAT_ID 967/967 (helper forced; also J=128 forced). Greedy --temp 0, 4 prompts
  (397-6,311 tok) and a checkpoint save+restore test (cache_prompt, a 4,259-token cached prefix with divergent tails):
  text and top-5 logprobs bitwise identical to stock, with default --cache-ram and with --cache-ram 0.
Evidence: boltbeam-runs/llama-expert-table-20261111.md and boltbeam-runs/llama-expert-table-20261111/

